==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined in 1912 by Swiss psychiatrist [[w:Paul Bleuler|Paul Bleuler]] (1857-1939) from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|autismus|lang=la}} from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|αὐτός||self|tr=autos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{clinical psychology}} Abnormal [[self-absorption]], observable in early [[childhood]], characterised by lack of [[response]] to other humans and by limited ability or disinclination to [[communicate]]. Occasionally either of the terms [[autism spectrum disorder]] and "spectrum of autism" are used interchangably.

====Synonyms====
*[[mindblindness]]
*[[on the spectrum]] {{slang}}

====Derived terms====
* [[autistic]], [[autism spectrum disorder]]

